            <ArticleTitle>Left circumflex coronary artery bridging.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Myocardial bridging most frequently occurs on the left anterior descending coronary artery and may cause ischemia and related complications. Right coronary artery myocardial bridges (MB) are rare. We report a patient with an unusual coronary bridge, a left circumflex coronary artery bridge, who presented with exercise-induced angina pectoris that was relieved with medical therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
